## 1. The observation (Nexus) and the confirmation (Architect)

The new Conv-rank failure is not a novel pathology — it is the latest member of a family we have been documenting since the original proof-of-concept. The tell is in Grok's own diagnosis: `read_model` holds the decoder's convs at legal **3D×3D**; inside the **GPU ProgramBuilder** the filters emerge as 4D `[512,1090,1,1]` against still-3D data `[1,1090,192]`. The plugin upranked the weights toward its 4D-native layout and failed to uprank the activations — a **half-applied rank-lifting transformation**. Our very first monolith surgery (3D→4D Resize lift) was us performing, by hand, the uprank the plugin could not perform for Interpolate. Same seam, five years of déjà vu compressed into one project.

