**Unifying claim for the filings:** the intel_gpu plugin is 4D-native (bfyx) at its core, and **rank-3 graphs — 1D-convolutional audio models as a class — repeatedly hit its weak seam**: missing rank-3 kernels (#1), rank propagation failures (#2), internally inconsistent shape transforms (#3, #5), and reference-kernel fallback for the rank-3-origin shapes that do compile (#4). Kokoro is not unlucky; it is representative. TTS/vocoder workloads on Intel iGPU will keep tripping this seam until it is addressed as a family.

## 3. Filing-pack implications (design, for the Nexus-scheduled filing session)

1. **File the conv-rank issue against OpenVINO (primary), per Grok's disposition** — and the family framing strengthens the plugin-blame case beyond the one-op repro's "undetermined": same file compiles on CPU; `read_model` ranks consistent; minimal uprank patterns succeed; failure localized inside the GPU build path; and the plugin has a documented history (#1–#3) of exactly this transform class on this hardware. Repro = full `kokoro_decoder_t96_edge_dynamo.onnx`, working minimals attached as contrast (Grok's recommended narrative adopted verbatim).
2. **Cross-link all filings under the family thesis.** Each issue gets a short "related reports" section citing the others plus one paragraph of the §2 claim. Point bugs invite point triage; a documented pattern across five manifestations, two graphs, and one host invites an owner. The shape-JIT filing keeps its separate identity (dynamic-shape `ImplementationsCache`, MIOpen contrast) but joins the cross-link ring — it is the *dynamic-shape* face of the same "audio models are second-class on intel_gpu" story.
3. **Filing count: four.** Shape-JIT (with static-T contrast data), f16 MatMul, f32 ref-conv (now two-graph, profile-backed), conv-rank (new). The optional PyTorch-side note stays secondary per notes/31 — no one-op exporter smoking gun exists, and we say so plainly.
4. **One sentence of restraint for all drafts:** we report the family as measured behavior on one host and one model family; we do not claim to know the plugin internals' root cause. The evidence earns the pattern claim; humility keeps the filings credible.

